Up until last year, I was a student of Scarborough College, now I just work
there.  It's true that students aren't allowed to post news.  The system
administrators claim that they're responsible for EVERYTHING that goes out
from our machines, whether it includes a disclaimer or not.  Hence if
someone was being a real turd and posted garbage all over the net, they
(sys. admins.) would be held responsible.

I suspect that if students had the ability to post news, they wouldn't.
The fear factor here at Scarborough is too great!  If you do something, you
don't get a warning.  Your account is immediately locked.  For posting this
article, I'll probably receive some flack.  I'll probably lose the privilege
to post news.

Regarding IRC:  One of the system administrators here submitted a report to
a divison chair.  When making reference to IRC, he had the following in
brackets "a net sex program".  Obviously none of the sys. admins. know what
IRC is, because this is a totally insane description of IRC.  It's like
saying USENET is exclusively used for distributing pornography.

By the way, students are NOT allowed to display images on their X-terminals
either!  It is unacademic to personalize ones working environment.  For
example, a student changed the title of his Xclock to "The F**ing time is"
and had his account suspended.
